kim akurvata sañjaya\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":191,\"bb\":184,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b184/\",\"shadow_value\":\"dhṛtarāṣṭraḥ uvāca – King Dhṛtarāṣṭra said; dharma-kṣetre – in the place of pilgrimage; kuru-kṣetre – in the place named Kurukṣetra; samavetāḥ – assembled; yuyutsavaḥ – desiring to fight; māmakāḥ – my party (sons); pāṇḍavāḥ – the sons of Pāṇḍu; ca – and; eva – certainly; kim – what; akurvata – did they do; sañjaya – O Sañjaya.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"dhṛtarāṣṭraḥ uvāca\",\"translation\":\"King Dhṛtarāṣṭra said\"},{\"word\":\"dharma-kṣetre\",\"translation\":\"in the place of pilgrimage\"},{\"word\":\"kuru-kṣetre\",\"translation\":\"in the place named Kurukṣetra\"},{\"word\":\"samavetāḥ\",\"translation\":\"assembled\"},{\"word\":\"yuyutsavaḥ\",\"translation\":\"desiring to fight\"},{\"word\":\"māmakāḥ\",\"translation\":\"my party (sons)\"},{\"word\":\"pāṇḍavāḥ\",\"translation\":\"the sons of Pāṇḍu\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"kim\",\"translation\":\"what\"},{\"word\":\"akurvata\",\"translation\":\"did they do\"},{\"word\":\"sañjaya\",\"translation\":\"O Sañjaya\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":192,\"bb\":185,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b185/\",\"body_value\":\"Dhṛtarāṣṭra said: O Sañjaya, after my sons and the sons of Pāṇḍu assembled in the place of pilgrimage at Kurukṣetra, desiring to fight, what did they do?\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":193,\"bb\":186,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b186/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":194,\"bb\":187,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b187/\",\"body_value\":\"The topics discussed by Dhṛtarāṣṭra and Sañjaya, as described in the Mahābhārata, form the basic principle for this great philosophy. It is understood that this philosophy evolved on the Battlefield of Kurukṣetra, which is a sacred place of pilgrimage from the immemorial time of the Vedic age. It was spoken by the Lord when He was present personally on this planet for the guidance of mankind.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":195,\"bb\":188,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b188/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":196,\"bb\":189,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/1/b189/\",\"body_value\":\"Both the Pāṇḍavas and the sons of Dhṛtarāṣṭra belong to the same family, but Dhṛtarāṣṭra’s mind is disclosed herein. He deliberately claimed only his sons as Kurus, and he separated the sons of Pāṇḍu from the family heritage. One can thus understand the specific position of Dhṛtarāṣṭra in his relationship with his nephews, the sons of Pāṇḍu. As in the paddy field the unnecessary plants are taken out, so it is expected from the very beginning of these topics that in the religious field of Kurukṣetra, where the father of religion, Śrī Kṛṣṇa, was present, the unwanted plants like Dhṛtarāṣṭra’s son Duryodhana and others would be wiped out and the thoroughly religious persons, headed by Yudhiṣṭhira, would be established by the Lord. This is the significance of the words dharma-kṣetre and kuru-kṣetre, apart from their historical and Vedic importance.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 1.1\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 1.1\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9c